# Agent Lifecycle

Governs how an agent starts up, stays coordinated during work, and shuts down
cleanly.

Holly's delivery model is the **swarm**. One long-lived **Orchestrator** runs in
a single window, owns a session, and dispatches **bounded workers** via
`runSubagent` (VS Code) / `Agent` (Claude Code). Each worker does exactly one
assigned task, returns a structured report, and exits. There are **no persistent
worker windows, no chat-channel onboarding, no BEGIN / SIGN-OFF handshake, and no
`holly chat wait` coordination loop.** Coordination is the Orchestrator dispatching and
collecting reports — not agents talking to each other over chat.

## When to Use

- At the start of any agent session (automatically via the `SessionStart` hook, or manually).
- To understand how the session hooks (boot / activity / idle) fit the swarm model.
- When debugging lifecycle issues (stale sessions, missed handoffs, orphaned state).
- When onboarding a new agent type.

## Decision: which lifecycle applies to you?

```text
Were you invoked as a bounded worker (runSubagent / Agent)?
  YES --> "Bounded Worker" — inherit context, do ONE task, return a report, exit.
  NO  --> "Orchestrator / Primary" — you own a session for the whole delivery.
```

